<!--meta {"lead": "A description list shows the facts of one record as label and value pairs: an appointment's service, time, estimate and location. Facts scan faster as pairs than as sentences.", "description": "Horizontal (label beside value) and stacked description lists, responsive from 640px, in both themes.", "pills": ["Native <code>&lt;dl&gt;</code>", "Status: stable"], "variants": "horizontal, stacked", "states": "default, value missing, value pending", "sources": []} -->
<section class="ds-section" id="overview"><h2><a href="#overview">Overview</a></h2>
  <p>Use a description list for the fields of a single record that people read rather than edit: the appointment detail, the review step of a booking, the account summary. Use a <a href="table.html">table</a> to compare several records, and a <a href="form-field.html">form</a> when the values are editable.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Horizontal</b> (<code>.dl</code>): labels in a narrow column beside values from 640px; stacked on phones.</li>
    <li><b>Stacked</b> (<code>.dl--stacked</code>): label above value at every width, for asides and narrow cards.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="anatomy"><h2><a href="#anatomy">Anatomy</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-anatomy">
    <figure class="ds-anatomy__figure">
      <dl class="dl" style="width: 100%;"><dt>Preferred time</dt><dd>Sat 24 Oct · 10:00 am</dd></dl>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 6%; top: 30%;" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 48%; top: 30%;" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
    </figure>
    <ol class="ds-anatomy__list">
      <li><div><b>Term</b><small><code>&lt;dt&gt;</code>: label type in <code>--color-fg-muted</code>; sized to its longest label (<code>max-content</code>).</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Value</b><small><code>&lt;dd&gt;</code>: body type in <code>--color-fg-default</code>; can hold a badge or a link.</small></div></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="variants"><h2><a href="#variants">Variants</a></h2>
  {{example:[start]Horizontal in a detail card; stacked in an aside. Resize below 640px to see the horizontal list stack.}}
<section class="card" style="flex: 2 1 20rem;" aria-labelledby="dl-ex-1">
  <h3 id="dl-ex-1">Request HP-1048</h3>
  <dl class="dl">
    <dt>Status</dt><dd><span class="badge badge--warning">Awaiting reply</span></dd>
    <dt>Service</dt><dd>Medium knotless braids</dd>
    <dt>Braider</dt><dd><a href="../../mocks/pages/braider-profile/default.html">Nia Okafor</a></dd>
    <dt>Preferred time</dt><dd>Sat 24 Oct · 10:00 am · about 5 hours</dd>
    <dt>Estimate</dt><dd>$180–$240</dd>
    <dt>Final price</dt><dd class="text-muted">Nia confirms after accepting</dd>
    <dt>Location</dt><dd class="text-muted">Shared after Nia accepts</dd>
  </dl>
</section>
<aside class="card" style="flex: 1 1 12rem;" aria-labelledby="dl-ex-2">
  <h3 id="dl-ex-2">Before you book</h3>
  <dl class="dl dl--stacked">
    <dt>Service area</dt><dd>Toronto West</dd>
    <dt>Typical duration</dt><dd>5 hours</dd>
    <dt>Knotless braids</dt><dd>From $180</dd>
  </dl>
</aside>
  {{/example}}
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sizes" data-na="One size; type follows the body and label roles."><h2><a href="#sizes">Sizes</a></h2></section>

<section class="ds-section" id="states"><h2><a href="#states">States</a></h2>
  <p>Description lists are static. Values have three content states: present, pending (not known yet, said in words, muted) and missing (an inline danger status, then a retry link that names what it retries). A fact the record does not have is omitted, term and value. Never leave a value blank or show a dash alone.</p>
  <div class="ds-matrix"><table>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Variant</th><th scope="col">Present</th><th scope="col">Pending</th><th scope="col">Missing</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Horizontal</th>
        <td><dl class="dl"><dt>Estimate</dt><dd>$180–$240</dd></dl></td>
        <td><dl class="dl"><dt>Final price</dt><dd class="text-muted">Nia confirms after accepting</dd></dl></td>
        <td><dl class="dl"><dt>Reviews</dt><dd><span class="inline-status inline-status--danger">Couldn’t load</span> · <a href="../../mocks/pages/braider-profile/partial.html">Retry reviews</a></dd></dl></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Stacked</th>
        <td><dl class="dl dl--stacked"><dt>Estimate</dt><dd>$180–$240</dd></dl></td>
        <td><dl class="dl dl--stacked"><dt>Final price</dt><dd class="text-muted">Nia confirms after accepting</dd></dl></td>
        <td><dl class="dl dl--stacked"><dt>Reviews</dt><dd><span class="inline-status inline-status--danger">Couldn’t load</span> · <a href="../../mocks/pages/braider-profile/partial.html">Retry reviews</a></dd></dl></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <h3>Both themes</h3>
  {{themes}}<dl class="dl"><dt>Service</dt><dd>Medium knotless braids</dd><dt>Preferred time</dt><dd>Sat 24 Oct · 10:00 am</dd><dt>Estimate</dt><dd>$180–$240</dd></dl>{{/themes}}
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="responsive"><h2><a href="#responsive">Responsive behaviour</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Below <code>--layout-breakpoint-sm</code> (640px) <code>.dl</code> stacks: each term sits above its value with 8px after the value.</li>
    <li>From 640px the term column is as wide as the longest label and the value takes the rest; rows are 8px apart with 24px between columns.</li>
    <li>Long values wrap inside their column; keep terms to three words so the label column stays narrow.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="theming"><h2><a href="#theming">Theming</a></h2>
  <p>Terms read <code>--color-fg-muted</code>, values <code>--color-fg-default</code>; spacing reads <code>--space-1/2/3/6</code>. No component tokens: override the semantic text colours if a surface needs it.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="accessibility"><h2><a href="#accessibility">Accessibility</a></h2>
  <h3>Role and pattern</h3>
  <p>Native <code>&lt;dl&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;dt&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;dd&gt;</code>: screen readers announce the list and pair count. Do not wrap pairs in extra <code>&lt;div&gt;</code>s that break the grid, and do not fake pairs with paragraphs and bold text.</p>
  <h3>Keyboard</h3>
  <table class="ds-table ds-keys"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Key</th><th scope="col">Action</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><kbd>Tab</kbd></td><td>Reaches only links or buttons inside values; the list itself is not focusable.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <h3>Focus</h3>
  <p>Not focusable; links inside values use the shared ring.</p>
  <h3>Labelling</h3>
  <p>The card heading above names the record. Terms are the labels; do not repeat them in the value ("Estimate: $180–$240" under "Estimate").</p>
  <h3>Contrast</h3>
  <div class="ds-example__canvas ds-example__canvas--stack" style="padding: 0; gap: var(--space-2);">
    {{pair:Term on card|--color-fg-muted|--color-bg-surface|4.5}}
    {{pair:Value on card|--color-fg-default|--color-bg-surface|4.5}}
    {{pair:Term in dialog|--color-fg-muted|--color-bg-surface-raised|4.5}}
  </div>
  <h3>Motion</h3>
  <p>None.</p>
  <h3>Touch</h3>
  <p>Links inside values keep a 24px target.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="content"><h2><a href="#content">Content</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Terms are short nouns in sentence case, no colon: "Preferred time", "Estimate".</li>
    <li>Values use the product formats: "Sat 24 Oct · 10:00 am", "$180–$240", "about 5 hours".</li>
    <li>Say why a value is not known yet ("Shared after Nia accepts") instead of leaving it blank.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="do-dont"><h2><a href="#do-dont">Do and don't</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-dodont">
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><dl class="dl"><dt>Preferred time</dt><dd>Sat 24 Oct · 10:00 am</dd><dt>Estimate</dt><dd>$180–$240</dd><dt>Location</dt><dd class="text-muted">Shared after Nia accepts</dd></dl></div><figcaption>Lay appointment facts out as pairs.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas ds-example__canvas--stack"><p><strong>Sat 24 Oct · 10:00 am</strong> with Nia Okafor</p><p>Estimated price: $180–$240. Nia will confirm the final price.</p><p>Location shared after Nia accepts.</p></div><figcaption>Bury the facts in sentences, as the appointment-detail mock does; time, price and place are hard to scan.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><dl class="dl"><dt>Final price</dt><dd class="text-muted">Nia confirms after accepting</dd></dl></div><figcaption>Explain a pending value.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><dl class="dl"><dt>Final price</dt><dd>—</dd></dl></div><figcaption>Show a lone dash; it is read as "dash" and says nothing.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="tokens"><h2><a href="#tokens">Tokens</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-table-wrap"><table class="ds-table">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Part</th><th scope="col">Token</th><th scope="col">Light</th><th scope="col">Dark</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {{tok:Term|--color-fg-muted}}
      {{tok:Value|--color-fg-default}}
      {{tok:Term font|--text-label}}
      {{tok:Value font|--text-body}}
      {{tok:Row gap / column gap|--space-2|--space-6}}
      {{tok:Stack breakpoint|--layout-breakpoint-sm}}
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="code"><h2><a href="#code">Code</a></h2>
  <pre><code>&lt;dl class="dl"&gt;
  &lt;dt&gt;Service&lt;/dt&gt;&lt;dd&gt;Medium knotless braids&lt;/dd&gt;
  &lt;dt&gt;Preferred time&lt;/dt&gt;&lt;dd&gt;Sat 24 Oct · 10:00 am&lt;/dd&gt;
  &lt;dt&gt;Estimate&lt;/dt&gt;&lt;dd&gt;$180–$240&lt;/dd&gt;
&lt;/dl&gt;</code></pre>
  <table class="ds-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Class</th><th scope="col">Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><code>.dl</code></td><td>Stacked below 640px; term and value columns from 640px.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.dl--stacked</code></td><td>Term above value at every width.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sources"><h2><a href="#sources">Sources</a></h2>
  <p>Core-set component: the mocks state these facts as prose. It is recommended for:</p>
  <ul>
    {{mock:pages/appointment-detail/default|time, estimate and location as sentences}}
    {{mock:pages/appointment-detail/success|confirmed estimate and studio address as sentences}}
    {{mock:dialogs/request-review/default|review step that should list the request's details}}
  </ul>
  <p>Drift recorded: appointment facts were written as prose ("Sat 24 Oct · 10:00 am with Nia Okafor", "Estimated price: …") rather than label and value pairs; the kit's <code>.dl</code> kept two columns at 360px, squeezing values (now stacked below 640px).</p>
</section>
